# OpenClaw — Master Specification

> **Read this before touching any code.** This document is the ground truth for what OpenClaw is, how it works, and how to build it correctly.

---

## 1. What OpenClaw Is (Non-Negotiable)

OpenClaw is a **factory framework** that empowers organizations to spin up their own AI workforces.

**The factory builds AI SaaS products. Organizations are the customers. Their AI workforce is the product.**

The law firm vertical is the **first proof-of-concept** to validate the repeatable framework. It is not the product. It is the demonstration that the factory works.

Every future vertical — IR, marketing, HR, biotech, finance, legal — runs on **identical infrastructure** with different skill bundles installed.

### What the Platform Handles

- Model training pipeline (RAG adaptation, FAISS, eval harness)
- Multi-tenant Model Forge (workspaces, datasets, jobs, registry, deployments)
- Governance layer (human-in-loop, audit trace, privilege warnings)
- Benchmark integration (adversarial playbook, multi-LLM testing)
- ZOA, Archon, Kairos execution engines
- Skill generation, validation, and catalog (791+ skills)
- Per-tenant Gateway provisioning (Docker on Render)

### Forbidden Language

| Never say | Say instead |
|---|---|
| "Legal AI API" | "AI workforce factory" |
| "Law firm tool" | "First proof-of-concept vertical" |
| "Demo" | "Live" or "Production" |
| "API endpoints" | "Deployed AI workforce" |
| "Legal SaaS" | "SaaS-as-a-Service factory" |

