## 9. Database Schema (28 Tables)

### Core

`tenants`, `activity_entries`, `chat_messages`

### Skills

`skills`, `tenant_skills`, `skill_versions`, `skill_benchmarks`

### Connectors

`connectors`, `tenant_connectors` (AES-256-GCM encrypted credentials)

### Knowledge Graphs

`knowledge_graphs`, `graph_documents`, `graph_chunks` (tsvector + GIN index)

### Model Forge

`model_workspaces`, `model_datasets`, `dataset_versions`, `dataset_documents`, `training_jobs`, `training_job_artifacts`, `evaluation_runs`, `evaluation_metrics`, `model_registrations`, `model_versions`, `model_deployments`, `deployment_endpoints`, `model_usage_events`, `model_policies`, `model_approvals`

### Conventions

- All rows scoped by `tenant_id` — never query without it
- JSONB columns: `hyperparams`, `metadata`, `level_scores` — use `JSON.stringify()` on insert
- Status columns are text (not PostgreSQL enums)
- Tenant ID derived from Clerk userId: `tenant-${userId.replace(/[^a-z0-9]/gi, '-').toLowerCase().slice(0, 32)}`

